Appendix A: Complete Proofs of Principal Results

A.1 Proof of Proposition 1 (Persistent Lag Ratio)

Statement. If AI capability grows exponentially at rate $r_A$ and governance adapts linearly at rate $k_G$, then the ratio of governance lag to AI capability converges to:

\rho^* = \frac{r_A}{r_A + k_G}

Proof. We begin with the exponential growth model in the pre-saturation regime:

A(t) = A_0 e^{r_A t}, \quad t \ge 0

The governance adaptation equation is:

\frac{dG}{dt} = k_G(A - G)

This is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation. We solve it using the integrating factor method. Rewriting:

\frac{dG}{dt} + k_G G = k_G A(t) = k_G A_0 e^{r_A t}

The integrating factor is $\mu(t) = e^{k_G t}$. Multiplying both sides:

\frac{d}{dt}\left[G(t) e^{k_G t}\right] = k_G A_0 e^{(r_A + k_G)t}

Integrating from 0 to $t$:

G(t) e^{k_G t} - G(0) = \frac{k_G A_0}{r_A + k_G}\left[e^{(r_A + k_G)t} - 1\right]

Therefore:

G(t) = G(0) e^{-k_G t} + \frac{k_G A_0}{r_A + k_G}\left[e^{r_A t} - e^{-k_G t}\right]

The governance lag is:

L(t) = A(t) - G(t) = A_0 e^{r_A t} - G(0) e^{-k_G t} - \frac{k_G A_0}{r_A + k_G}\left[e^{r_A t} - e^{-k_G t}\right]

L(t) = A_0 e^{r_A t}\left[1 - \frac{k_G}{r_A + k_G}\right] - e^{-k_G t}\left[G(0) - \frac{k_G A_0}{r_A + k_G}\right]

L(t) = A_0 e^{r_A t} \cdot \frac{r_A}{r_A + k_G} - e^{-k_G t}\left[G(0) - \frac{k_G A_0}{r_A + k_G}\right]

Now consider the lag ratio:

\rho(t) = \frac{L(t)}{A(t)} = \frac{A_0 e^{r_A t} \cdot \frac{r_A}{r_A + k_G} - e^{-k_G t}\left[G(0) - \frac{k_G A_0}{r_A + k_G}\right]}{A_0 e^{r_A t}}

\rho(t) = \frac{r_A}{r_A + k_G} - \frac{e^{-(r_A + k_G)t}}{A_0}\left[G(0) - \frac{k_G A_0}{r_A + k_G}\right]

As $t \to \infty$, the exponential term $e^{-(r_A + k_G)t} \to 0$ since $r_A + k_G > 0$. Therefore:

\rho^* = \lim_{t \to \infty} \rho(t) = \frac{r_A}{r_A + k_G}

Since $r_A > 0$ and $k_G > 0$, we have $\rho^* \in (0, 1)$. This completes the proof. $\blacksquare$

