A.3 Proof of Proposition 3 (Delay-Induced Lag Degradation)

Statement. The introduction of a governance response delay $\tau_d$ transforms the lag ratio from $\rho^* = r_A/(r_A + k_G)$ to:

\rho^*_{\text{delay}} = 1 - \frac{k_G e^{-r_A\tau_d}}{r_A + k_G}

Proof. The delayed governance equation is:

\frac{dG(t)}{dt} = k_G [A(t - \tau_d) - G(t)]

with exponential capability growth $A(t) = A_0 e^{r_A t}$.

For $t \ge \tau_d$, we have:

A(t - \tau_d) = A_0 e^{r_A(t - \tau_d)} = A_0 e^{-r_A \tau_d} e^{r_A t}

The DDE becomes:

\frac{dG}{dt} + k_G G = k_G A_0 e^{-r_A \tau_d} e^{r_A t}

Using the integrating factor $e^{k_G t}$:

\frac{d}{dt}[G(t) e^{k_G t}] = k_G A_0 e^{-r_A \tau_d} e^{(r_A + k_G)t}

Integrating from 0 to $t$ (note that the integration is valid even for $t < \tau_d$ if we use the initial history):

G(t) e^{k_G t} - G(0) = \frac{k_G A_0 e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G}\left[e^{(r_A + k_G)t} - 1\right]

G(t) = G(0) e^{-k_G t} + \frac{k_G A_0 e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G}\left[e^{r_A t} - e^{-k_G t}\right]

The steady-state (large $t$) behavior is:

G(t) \sim \frac{k_G A_0 e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G} e^{r_A t} = \frac{k_G e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G} A(t)

The lag ratio is:

\rho^*_{\text{delay}} = \lim_{t \to \infty} \frac{A(t) - G(t)}{A(t)} = 1 - \lim_{t \to \infty} \frac{G(t)}{A(t)} = 1 - \frac{k_G e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G}

This completes the proof. $\blacksquare$

