A.4 Proof of Proposition 4 (Feasibility Threshold)

Statement. For a prescribed maximum acceptable lag ratio $\rho_{\max} \in (0,1)$, the governance response delay must satisfy:

\tau_d < \frac{-\ln(1 - \rho_{\max})}{r_A} \equiv \tau_{\text{feas}}

If $\tau_d \ge \tau_{\text{feas}}$, no finite governance adaptation rate $k_G$ can achieve $\rho^*_{\text{delay}} \le \rho_{\max}$.

Proof. From the delayed lag ratio:

\rho^*_{\text{delay}} = 1 - \frac{k_G e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G}

We require $\rho^*_{\text{delay}} \le \rho_{\max}$:

1 - \frac{k_G e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G} \le \rho_{\max}

\frac{k_G e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G} \ge 1 - \rho_{\max}

Since $r_A + k_G > 0$ and $k_G > 0$:

k_G e^{-r_A \tau_d} \ge (1 - \rho_{\max})(r_A + k_G)

k_G [e^{-r_A \tau_d} - (1 - \rho_{\max})] \ge (1 - \rho_{\max}) r_A

For this inequality to be satisfiable with $k_G > 0$, we require:

e^{-r_A \tau_d} - (1 - \rho_{\max}) > 0

e^{-r_A \tau_d} > 1 - \rho_{\max}

Taking natural logarithms (valid since both sides are positive):

-r_A \tau_d > \ln(1 - \rho_{\max})

Since $0 < 1 - \rho_{\max} < 1$, we have $\ln(1 - \rho_{\max}) < 0$. Dividing by $-r_A < 0$ flips the inequality:

\tau_d < \frac{-\ln(1 - \rho_{\max})}{r_A}

This is the feasibility condition. If it is violated, the left-hand side of the inequality $k_G [e^{-r_A \tau_d} - (1 - \rho_{\max})] \ge (1 - \rho_{\max}) r_A$ has a non-positive coefficient for $k_G$ while the right-hand side is positive, making the inequality unsatisfiable for any $k_G > 0$. $\blacksquare$

