Appendix F: Worked Examples and Numerical Illustrations

F.1 Persistent Lag Ratio (Instantaneous Adaptation)

Parameters: $r_A = 0.69 \text{ yr}^{-1}$ (annual doubling), $k_G = 1.0 \text{ yr}^{-1}$.

Lag ratio:
\rho^* = \frac{r_A}{r_A + k_G} = \frac{0.69}{0.69 + 1.0} = \frac{0.69}{1.69} \approx 0.408

Interpretation: Governance institutions track approximately 59.2% of AI capability growth, with a persistent 40.8% lag.

F.2 Delayed Lag Ratio

Parameters: $r_A = 0.69 \text{ yr}^{-1}$, $k_G = 1.0 \text{ yr}^{-1}$, $\tau_d = 1 \text{ yr}$.

Lag ratio:
\rho^*_{\text{delay}} = 1 - \frac{k_G e^{-r_A \tau_d}}{r_A + k_G} = 1 - \frac{1.0 \cdot e^{-0.69}}{1.69} = 1 - \frac{0.502}{1.69} \approx 0.703

Comparison: The delay increases the lag ratio from 0.408 to 0.703, a 72% degradation in tracking efficiency.

F.3 Feasibility Threshold

Parameters: $\rho_{\max} = 0.1$, $r_A = 0.69 \text{ yr}^{-1}$.

Feasibility:
\tau_{\text{feas}} = \frac{-\ln(0.9)}{0.69} \approx \frac{0.105}{0.69} \approx 0.152 \text{ yr} \approx 55 \text{ days}

Implication: To achieve a 10% maximum lag ratio with AI capability doubling annually, governance institutions must detect and respond to capability changes within 55 days. This is faster than most current human institutional processes.

F.4 Hopf Bifurcation Threshold

Parameters: $r_A = 0.69 \text{ yr}^{-1}$, $k_G = 2.0 \text{ yr}^{-1}$.

Critical frequency:
\omega_c = \sqrt{k_G^2 - r_A^2} = \sqrt{4.0 - 0.476} = \sqrt{3.524} \approx 1.877 \text{ yr}^{-1}

Critical delay:
\tau_c = \frac{\arccos(0.69/2.0)}{1.877} = \frac{\arccos(0.345)}{1.877} \approx \frac{1.218}{1.877} \approx 0.649 \text{ yr} \approx 237 \text{ days}

Implication: With a governance adaptation rate twice the AI growth rate, the system becomes oscillatory if the response delay exceeds approximately 237 days.

F.5 Volatility Variance Tax

Parameters: $r_A = 0.69 \text{ yr}^{-1}$, $\sigma = 0.3 \text{ yr}^{-1/2}$, $\tau_d = 1 \text{ yr}$.

Deterministic penalty: $e^{-r_A \tau_d} = e^{-0.69} \approx 0.502$

Stochastic penalty: $e^{-\sigma^2 \tau_d} = e^{-0.09} \approx 0.914$

Combined penalty: $e^{-(r_A + \sigma^2/2)\tau_d} = e^{-(0.69 + 0.045)} \approx e^{-0.735} \approx 0.479$

Interpretation: The volatility adds an additional 2.3 percentage points of tracking degradation on top of the deterministic delay penalty.

